From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANYBOOK: GKI: x86: Add anybook_amd KMI symbol list

Symbols that the AnyBook AMD vendor modules (//devices/anybook) need
from vmlinux and from GKI modules. Generated with

  tools/bazel run //devices/anybook:anybook_amd_x86_64_abi_update_symbol_list

and merged into the GKI exports through x86_64_additional_kmi_symbol_lists.
Adding symbols only adds exports; no existing KMI symbol changes.

AnyBook-local, not in ACK. See docs/kernel.md in the AnyBook repo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Iee05da30818a9fd4f942053e1f76272002c97f96
---
 BUILD.bazel                    |    1 +
 gki/x86_64/symbols/anybook_amd | 2113 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 2114 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gki/x86_64/symbols/anybook_amd

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index 6ceea79295f4..679f1652429e 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -312,6 +312,7 @@ filegroup(
     name = "x86_64_additional_kmi_symbol_lists",
     srcs = [
         # keep sorted
+        "gki/x86_64/symbols/anybook_amd",
         "gki/x86_64/symbols/desktop",
         "gki/x86_64/symbols/kunit",
         "gki/x86_64/symbols/virtual_device",
